{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal","id":1018603,"title":"Why are the Seers such a big deal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-17T16:10:31-08:00","id":1018603,"title":"Why are the Seers such a big deal?","content":"Where does their temporal power come from (that the Pentacle couldn't match or surpass them anyway)?<br /> <br /> Yes I know they worship the Exarchs, and/thus they get Prelacies etc - but aren't they outnumbered by the Pentacle and constantly infighting?<br /> So why would they be able to amass the resources/connections they're described as having? Are the Tetrarchs/Exarchs continually casting Imperial spells to create wealth etc?<br /> <br /> [Apologies if addressed before]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11932-jerkajerka","name":"jerkajerka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T16:23:39-08:00","id":1018607,"title":"","content":"One, they're sponsored by the Exarchs who are basically the winners of the Ascension War and this sponsorship leads to more benefits than simply developing Prelacies. For instance they can summon Supernal backup in the form of Ochemata. Two, archmasters typically when they break the Threshold go ahead and sign onto the Pax Arcana which involves only indirectly affecting Mage politics with their ridiculous levels of power. The Archmasters from the Seers are under fewer restrictions in this regard and all four of the Ministries basically have at least one Archmaster at the top directly contributing to the Seers cause. Three, the Fallen World has basically been restructured, retroactively, by the Exarchs to make an orginization dependent on tyranny and backstabbing and the like to be more able to succeed so the Seers are basically always on their home turf. Four, the Seers are bigger than any one Order and though divided by Ministries all of those Ministries have the same fundamental goal of obeying the Exarchs. The Orders by contrast have multiple and sometimes conflicting goals and the Seers can put in wedges easily enough to maintain a divide and stalemate scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T16:37:55-08:00","id":1018612,"title":"","content":"The dudes in charge of reality are their bosses. It's like insider trading on the biggest scale possible, or like how in real life you can get a lot further if the cops are on your team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T17:15:34-08:00","id":1018622,"title":"","content":"They've also got access to really powerful artifacts through their Exarch masters.<br /> <br /> It helps that no one really existed that was a dedicated enemy to them until fairly recently, and even then the Free Council aren't all gung-ho about taking them down. And while some of the Orders have overlaps in power structures of the world, they don't entirely infringe on them as a real competitor except for other Seers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T19:09:41-08:00","id":1018646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1018607#post1018607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One, they're sponsored by the Exarchs who are basically the winners of the Ascension War and this sponsorship leads to more benefits than simply developing Prelacies. For instance they can summon Supernal backup in the form of Ochemata. Two, archmasters typically when they break the Threshold go ahead and sign onto the Pax Arcana which involves only indirectly affecting Mage politics with their ridiculous levels of power. The Archmasters from the Seers are under fewer restrictions in this regard and all four of the Ministries basically have at least one Archmaster at the top directly contributing to the Seers cause. Three, the Fallen World has basically been restructured, retroactively, by the Exarchs to make an orginization dependent on tyranny and backstabbing and the like to be more able to succeed so the Seers are basically always on their home turf. Four, the Seers are bigger than any one Order and though divided by Ministries all of those Ministries have the same fundamental goal of obeying the Exarchs. The Orders by contrast have multiple and sometimes conflicting goals and the Seers can put in wedges easily enough to maintain a divide and stalemate scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Correction, the Free Council is bigger. Not that much, though, and they don't have nearly the amount of fronts or puppet strings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T20:53:05-08:00","id":1018670,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that game works perfectly well without Seers (though you need to rework Free Councils conception slightly). In general, Seers seem to exist to make Pentacle more heroic and bring out what's best in it by contrast. If you remove or downplay Seers, it might be wise to either use another group of Mages representing dangers of &quot;evil&quot; (like Scelesti, Banishers, etc, though they represent different perversions of the Wisdom), or - which is personally my favorite - make Pentacle much more asshole-ish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T21:04:02-08:00","id":1018674,"title":"","content":"The Seers are there to prove that you can still be a total asshole while being both enlightened and Wise. Banishers, Scelesti, Mad Ones and Liches have something clearly wrong about them - enough to be a warning to what you can become, but not as a warning to what you are right now. Left-Handed are somewhere between &quot;moral dissonance&quot; and &quot;political scapegoat&quot;, so they're a bit more ambiguous.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T22:32:01-08:00","id":1018695,"title":"","content":"I feel like a lot of the posts here are forgetting that the Seers have something that pretty much no other Order does: An actual, functional hierarchy.<br /> <br /> ... Alright, functional is overstating it somewhat - Seers pretty much have &quot;Insert knife here&quot; painted on the backs of their jackets - but at the end of the day, there <i>is</i> a fairly clear structure. Every Seer agrees that, yeah, they're worshiping <i>those guys</i>, and when <i>those guys</i> give an order, everyone follows it. On this point, the Exarchs are explicit; they have their Ministers with whom they commune quite directly and who receive orders from the very gods themselves telling them to get their shit together and, from Ministers this information flows to Tetrarchs, many of whom are archmasters who commune with the gods themselves as well, and from Tetrarchs to Prelates who have a literal portion of their soul dedicated to their patron Exarch...<br /> <br /> The point is that, while everyone might think they're a better pick for who is in charge, there's no dispute about them ultimately all belonging to the same organization and that <i>someone</i> is in charge of the whole thing. That means the Great Ministers can direct - in broad strokes - the fates of entire nations or declare &quot;Fuck that one magister in particular&quot; and turn the resources of <i>hundreds</i> of Mages towards a singular goal.<br /> <br /> Even the most adamantly anti-Seer thearch must look upon what the Seers have accomplished and feel at least a <i>little</i> envy.<br /> <br /> Never underestimate the power of having everyone on the same page. Even setting aside that the Seers occasionally have ochema drop in for a quick &quot;Let's make Machiavelli's ghost shit his pants&quot; tea party, or that just about every Seer pylon has at least one profane urim (and may in fact have several), or that the Seers often have special slaves like the Myrmidons or the horrifying wandering souls that serve the Eye, the Seers actually have the resources to make their conspiracies truly international in the ways not even <i>one</i> of the Orders has ever managed.<br /> <br /> The last time the Silver Ladder held a Great Convocation (I think that's the one) that got the Awakened on the same page, it was because there was an entirely new Order emerging. Since then, most Convocations are &quot;Let's go meet the neighbours&quot; and amount to little beyond the local Caucuses saying howdy. The Seers, meanwhile, can hold meetings like that any time they want to if necessary, and do, because God decided to tell their boss how to properly buckle the jackboot stamping on a human face forever.<br /> <br /> The Seers are a globe-spanning conspiracy that manages to put its resources to a common purpose and the only reason they've not utterly steamrolled the Pentacle is because they're too busy putting knives in their own backs.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Pentacle Orders over there fracture every time there's a disagreement about how to properly articulate a particular syllable of the true name of an Oracle that may not even exist. Unless you're a libertine. Then it's whether someone is a fascist (more traditionalist than me) or a senseless anarchist (more liberal than me).<br /> <br /> I had too much fun with my analogies for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":34}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T10:42:27-08:00","id":1018845,"title":"","content":"Also remember this - <b>Seers command Hierarchy</b>. They work ( and embedded ) living symbols of Tyranny and can always summon this. Their 'Words of Power' Yantra can be simply called 'Command'. Any Seer can invoke particular Exarch in his spell, and summon it's rule over world. Need help from Army? Just say a High Speech name of General and commanders on battlefield will be yours to obey. Need new cash? Quick prayers-request to Mammon, and money will fill your pockets. Seers can use those 'Words of Power' to usurp influence in Sleepers society on the Fallen World ( just see Ministry write-ups in <b>Seers of Throne</b> 1E Order book ). It's no wonder - after all, they engineered it that way..\ufeff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=odAcNQnaltY\" data-code=\"odAcNQnaltY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/odAcNQnaltY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T15:50:45-08:00","id":1018942,"title":"","content":"Yaaa, everyone else has pretty much summed the Seers up perfectly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would like to share my favorite analogy for the Seers of the Thone though, courtesy of Darker Days Radio. If the Exarchs are the wardens of the jail that is the Fallen World, then the Seers are the special privilege prisoners who are given lavish cells, the best food, HBO, and are promised their good behavior would lead them to a lesser jail time...in exchange for being the warden's eyes and ears amongst the other prisoners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T16:22:47-08:00","id":1018953,"title":"","content":"&quot;Why are the wizards who serve the closest thing to gods the world has and active seek to distract and burden the human race with suffering and oppression (and have successfully done so for hundreds of years) such a big deal?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T17:04:36-08:00","id":1018966,"title":"","content":"All that said, with their power, they seem more of a passive antagonistic force, compared to more active things like the Pure or angels to demons. It's entirely possible for a mage to go their life without ever meeting one, and for a mage who has met several to never have had an encounter turn to violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T19:01:05-08:00","id":1018991,"title":"","content":"A cold war still has plenty of killing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T19:34:25-08:00","id":1019006,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that Seers have so many mundane resources because they have no laws or qualms about abusing Sleepers to take control of their organizations and assets from the shadows. Guardians of the Veil, Free Councilors and Thearchs are gonna look at you askance at best for abusing Sleepers in such a way that makes the world a worse place to live in. For Seers that's a Tuesday.<br /> <br /> Selfishness and tyranny pay out big for collaborators, both in magic and money and the influence the two can bring when guided by boundless ambition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T20:02:05-08:00","id":1019021,"title":"","content":"Every Pentacle Order will - at least publicly - look askew at you for abusing Sleepers for your own ends. They might excuse it when it serves a &quot;greater good&quot; - stealing mystical artifacts from Sleepers, forcing a political deal that benefits lots of people, etc. - but, for the most part, they have qualms against it. Seers are outright built on the premise of willfully treating people like chattel. You want something, take it. And if someone else wants something and people have to be hurt to give it to them, who cares?<br /> <br /> It's a dark world, baby, but not for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T05:04:01-08:00","id":1019168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1018695#post1018695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Seers, meanwhile, can hold meetings like that any time they want to if necessary, and do, because God decided to tell their boss how to properly buckle the jackboot stamping on a human face forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>As soon as is figure out how to set a signature I'm making this mine.<br /> <br /> Axelgear, your efforpost is amazing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T11:53:37-08:00","id":1019358,"title":"","content":"I am not sure why something I wrote in a mad frenzy at 1:30 in the morning is one of the most popular things I've ever written here, but I'm glad people are enjoying it, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T23:00:39-08:00","id":1020196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1019358#post1019358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure why something I wrote in a mad frenzy at 1:30 in the morning is one of the most popular things I've ever written here, but I'm glad people are enjoying it, thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>You have pretty awesome mad frenzies at 1:30 in the morning. Any chance I could manufacture these circumstances again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T04:50:56-08:00","id":1020284,"title":"","content":"I think that there's something else rather important that needs to be touched on. Well, Axelgear did touch on it, but it was in a manner that wasn't really expanded. Functional hierarchy or not*, one of the biggest things that being a Seer gets is actually better Mysteries at easy access. There are the Profane Urim, yes. There's the ochema as well. Its part of the draw of joining the Seers - easy access to powerful mysteries to study. Hells, the Exarchs themselves are a Mystery to study in the first place. And that doesn't touch on the orders that are handed down - each is an individual mystery that is divined and fulfills Obsessions.<br /> <br /> To put it simply, the Seers get handed easy power that indulges all their power fantasies with little effort. Not only do you get more toys to play with in the form of free Artifacts and specialized Supernal allies, but each and every one of those toys helps fulfill your Obsessions and grants you Arcane Beats. You are basically getting two kinds of power boosts for every gift, and at a low cost. Well, until your Exarch asks for something complex, but by then you're hooked into the life, willingly go out to fulfill your Obsession and get more Arcane experience points, then come back, get rewarded with more mysteries to look at, and get even more Arcane xp. Its a virtuous cycle that just keeps building. You have the mysteries, you grow more powerful, letting you acomplish more. You get an order now achievable, follow it, getting more mysteries that make you more powerful, which lets you get even more complex orders to acomplish. <br /> <br /> The sheer amount of magical resources that Seers have access to can't be denied. They grant an overwhelmingly huge advantage that mere numbers can't quite make up. Its the difference between being born the heir to a company, and trying to build a company from the ground up. Both are going to be in charge of a company, but clearly the former has a big advantage and more likely to be able to do more in the long run. <br /> <br /> * I think its important to remember that the Seers aren't a monolithic Order. In fact, calling them an Order is misleading in the first place - they're a series of Ministries that happen to all be called Seers. Its like saying the Diamond in reference to the SL, GotV, AA and Mys. Each Exarch has its own agenda that isn't necessarily united with other Exarchs. When the General says &quot;Jump,&quot; every Praetorean in the world will jump, sure, but no one in the Paternoster will. Hells, the Exarchs might not even <i>talk</i>. The Father could be the God-Machine, the Raptor could be the Dark Mother, the Eye could be an Asceneded archmage from Time Before, Helios could be the Nemesis, etc. Each concerned with only their own sphere of interest and staying out of each other's ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:16:10-08:00","id":1020302,"title":"","content":"Thank you for all your responses. I couldn't get my head around their backstabbing/infighting, and how they could mount a coherent response against the Pentacle... but thanks to the sheer flavour in this thread, a Pylon chronicle sounds like it could be tremendously fun. Even if I ignored the Pentacle...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11932-jerkajerka","name":"jerkajerka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T15:02:59-08:00","id":1020667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1020284#post1020284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Father could be the God-Machine, the Raptor could be the Dark Mother, the Eye could be an Asceneded archmage from Time Before, Helios could be the Nemesis, etc. Each concerned with only their own sphere of interest and staying out of each other's ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to remember that one if I ever want to run a more crossover-oriented Mage game. From the Seers' point of view, the Exarchs have many masks and might appear in different ways to their other servants. From an outside perspective, the Seers have been imprisoned by their own ideology and Obsessions, and the Iron Seals are like...50% a fake idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T18:01:47-08:00","id":1020733,"title":"","content":"Wait, I actually have a point that hasn't been brought up (sees MCN's post)...aaaw. Well what about (sees Caladriu's post) damnit! <br /> <br /> Ok, (double checks thread again) I think I actually got something to meaningfully contribute this time. And it's basically let's not forget about the possible origins for the Seers from To the Strongest in Dark Eras, or Neolithic Mage for that reason. <br /> <br /> Because the Exarchs are no more real than Atlantis is, which is to say that just like the Time Before has Supernal resonance with the idea of Atlantis thanks to the Diamond Orders, the Supernal Symbols for why reality is Fallen have resonance with the idea of the Exarchs because of the Seers. And that's because the Seers and the Diamond have similar origins, and that they're both really not that old in the grand scheme of things since they both supposedly came about during the Bronze Age. In the Neithic Age there was no concept of the Supernal, the Time Before, and definitely the Exarchs, and in the Bronze Age the closes concept that existed comparable to the Exarchs amongst the Great Cults (the Arcadian Mysteties specifically) was the Olympians (the symbols that improsoned the primordial shapes on Tartaris to usurp and rule their creation it their stead, and both maintain the world to their capricious whims while also ensuring the world isn't returned to primordial chaos should the &quot;Titans&quot; ever break free.) And in time the Olympions would be reimagined as the Exarchs because the Arcadian Mysyeries would eventually split into the Seers and the Ladder, but the actual term Exarch probably didn't come about until the Ladder first started crafting their Atlantean shadow name. <br /> <br /> And yet, the Supernal truth about what the Exarchs represent have always existed in the universe that exists now in the Chronicles of Darkness. Whether it's brutal forces of nature that are both mysterious and malicious that try to scour the Awakened as they try to break through to the Supernal, or capricious gods that delight in the entertainment of their mortal creations while demanding supplication and love despite their cruelty, to the forms were most familiar with: tyranical rules of reality from the Time Before who oppress mortal souls in an attempt to rule squash any chance of an awakened rebellion. No matter what form They take, there will always be foolish mortals and Mages who will try to use Them as a source of quick and easy power. Because They are powerful, and They do represent everything that keeps humanity from being something better than they are now. <br /> <br /> (P.S. Another fun thing to remember is that the Seers and the Diamond have something of a sinister relationship because they do share a groups shadow name. The Diamond needs servants of the Exarchs to rebel against to restore reality, and the Seers need rebels to squash an reaffirm their absolute rule. If at any time this relationship breaks down the Orders become in serious trouble, and that's why the Seers and Diamond have allied themselves with eachother in the past. Because they need eachother.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T20:46:04-08:00","id":1020772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1020284#post1020284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I think its important to remember that the Seers aren't a monolithic Order. In fact, calling them an Order is misleading in the first place - they're a series of Ministries that happen to all be called Seers. Its like saying the Diamond in reference to the SL, GotV, AA and Mys. Each Exarch has its own agenda that isn't necessarily united with other Exarchs. When the General says &quot;Jump,&quot; every Praetorean in the world will jump, sure, but no one in the Paternoster will.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I explain Mage Society to people, my outline for this part goes something like, &quot;So, there are three big Sects: the Diamond, the Council of Free Assemblies, and the Seers of the Throne. PCs come from the first two. If you're in the Diamond, you're part of one of these four Orders. If you're in the Council, then you come from an Assembly or a signatory Nameless Order. And any Seers belong to one of these Ministries. Also, apostates.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because that overarching organizing structure? It matters, even if it's <i>usually</i> just ceremonial, because this is Mage and those ceremonial symbols <i>matter</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T06:50:41-08:00","id":1020856,"title":"","content":"I compared it to the Diamond for a reason, Errol. Each Ministry is effectively a distinct Order, with different hiearchies and goals, but with the same kind of alliance as the Diamond Orders and the Assemblies have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T07:04:27-08:00","id":1020861,"title":"","content":"I would say that the Seers have the same goals, but different methods for accomplishing those goals. The Diamond on the other hand do have competing goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T08:12:35-08:00","id":1020885,"title":"","content":"Maybe? Only in the broadest sense? The thing to remember about Seers is that, as a whole, they're not driven by some desire to rule the world. They're driven by personal Obsessions and are just as Addicted to Mysteries as the next mage. Their main goal is to study things, to experiment, to mess with magic like every other Awakened. They end up actually ruling the world because that's what the Exarchs need to keep existing as Supernal symbols, and thus demand of their followers. Those who obey get their Obsessions and addictions fulfilled with ease, and free access to power as a result. The Exarchs stay in power for whatever reason (see below), and the lackies get their desires met. Its a symbiotic relationship. <br /> <br /> Now, in 2e, we don't know what the Exarchs are. The Psychopomp could be a Rank 10 Keroberus, a really ancient vampire, a death-spirit, or one of the Judges as easily as an ascended Death mage for all we know. And, to be frank, the answer probably will change depending on the needs of individual chronicles. What's important to note here is that, depending on which of those things the Exarch in question actually is, what the Exarch will demand of its followers will change. A Death Spirit will need its followers to do death-y things to feed it Essence. The keroberus will need essence from Memento Mori as much as it will need its Deep Laws fulfilled. And so on. Psychopomp-Seers will be executing missions that relate to fulfilling these death-based needs of their master. I mentioned earlier that, perhaps, the Father could be the God-Machine: the G-M does want control of the world, but only because its easier to build Infrastructure and fulfill its ultimate Mission, whatever that is. Meanwhile, ascended mages in the form of Supernal Symbols will likely have spells they want to cast, and each arch-level spell will require changing the world in different ways; again, a process that is expediated by control of humanity. <br /> <br /> Seers aren't vampires. They don't want control for its own sake or to fulfilll a psychological need (at least for the majority). Instead, they want these systems of control in place because the magic of the Exarchs / archmasters and the Seers all depend on these individual systems in some way. Its a means to acomplish an end. And that's why I say that the goals are different - even if we go with the Exarchs-are-all-former-mages idea, the spells cast and power attained are for different magical reasons. Everything with mages always, always, always comes back to magic in some way. But the thing with Supernal magic is that its so varied, and uses so many different angles, that there's lots of directions to take with it.<br /> <br /> And that's not to say there's not overlap - as many know, church and state work horrifyingly well together, and often overlap on using the same people. Normally, this would lead to a power struggle over a limited resource; however, because this resource (people) can be used in different ways without consuming them or used in conflicting ways, there's no reason to fight over the resource, but instead to share it, reinforcing a hold at a fraction of the effort.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, the point is that tyranny or causing suffering is closer to a Yantra than anything else. A tool, not a goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T08:25:56-08:00","id":1020893,"title":"","content":"I mean that the Seers have the same goal because they have a number of standing orders from the Exarchs that apply to all of them which is a distinct difference from the lack of a skeletal unity of purpose that the Diamond have. In that sense the Seers actually are closer to the Free Council who take multiple disparate groups and bring them all under the umbrella of their three main tenets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T09:09:59-08:00","id":1020913,"title":"","content":"Eh... The Diamond Orders all have points they agree on as well - they've even got a shared culture in the form of the Consilium. *shrugs* At this point, its going to be quibbling over details that we're clearly not going to agree on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T09:16:02-08:00","id":1020917,"title":"","content":"They have points they agree on, but none of those points are simple concise tenets shared on a global level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T09:56:54-08:00","id":1020932,"title":"","content":"The Diamond has a judicial system. The Seers have an executive system. The Council has a legislative system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T10:53:36-08:00","id":1020948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1020932#post1020932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Diamond has a judicial system. The Seers have an executive system. The Council has a legislative system.</div> </div> </div> </div>... and combined, they create GOVERNMENT! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Side topic - In Poland, for a year now, we have a problems with our government wanting to change <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitutional_Tribunal_(Poland)\" target=\"_blank\">Constitutional Tribunal</a> - as we heard more and more about it workings in media, I think it's great example of Consilium Council at work. Bonus points for going on meetings in funny toga's. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-22-2016, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T20:58:15-08:00","id":1021130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1020885#post1020885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, the point is that tyranny or causing suffering is closer to a Yantra than anything else. A tool, not a goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to address your whole post but this feels like a good summary of it so I'm gonna save space on quoting.<br /> <br /> This assessment doesn't sit with me. The precise why is a hard thing to put into words, because it's not <i>wrong</i>, per se, but it doesn't feel right.<br /> <br /> As best as I can summarize it, magic doesn't have a separation between an action and the thing itself. Symbols of Tyranny <i>are</i> Tyranny itself. When a violent servant of a dictatorial regime bludgeons a protestor with a cudgel, that <i>is</i> the General. When someone doesn't dare speak up in favour of liberty and equality for fear of what the neighbours might think, that <i>is</i> the Unity. There is no distinction between the Exarchs and the kind of tyranny they endorse. They are the thing which is itself.<br /> <br /> For that reason, tyranny <i>is</i> a goal, because the Exarchs seek tyranny. Whether that tyranny makes them more powerful or not is anyone's guess but tyranny isn't a means for them; it is a goal unto itself. That they rule and maintain hegemony is a part of the very idea that they are: Tyrants reign. If they did not reign, they would not be the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> (This is, incidentally, a part of why the Free Council believes hierarchy fosters the Lie: Hierarchies must enforce themselves on the unwilling, and the use of force to enforce one's will on another for the sake of controlling them is Exarchial in the extreme.)<br /> <br /> The Seers themselves, meanwhile, are Mages. As you say, that means they're addicted to the Mysteries; chasing their Obsessions. The Seers of the Throne offer that but, and this is critical, so does every Order. If all you want is a pile of occult lore, the Mysterium has your number. The difference that the Seers offer is that you get what they offer <i>cheap</i>. They don't require a year of your life spent researching a Mystery before you get your first initiation. The moment you prove you're a cold bastard by ruining someone's business or bribing a politician into killing a bill that helps people - the moment you can no longer hold onto any hope that you're not <i>really</i> hurting anyone - is the moment you get access to their shiny things. The funny thing about being a cold bastard is: It's easy. Tearing things down, hurting people, ruining lives; these things take seconds. Building is always harder than destroying.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Seers offer material rewards. While the more powerful Seers shift their gaze off of the mundane - mostly because they're so personally potent and involved in the Mysteries and jaded by excess and human misery at that point, that wealth holds no more promises or secrets - and into the esoteric, keep in mind that the lure of material wealth is a powerful one. A Mage who is promised a fat bank account is no more or less susceptible to the offer than anyone else, but it's more than just that. The Seers don't just give you wealth; they give you <i>privilege</i>. Money is great and all, but the Seers help you get to actually use it. It's not just &quot;Can you buy a fancy house?&quot;, it's &quot;Can you buy a fancy house next door to a crime lord who invites you over for a party, whereupon you shoot illegal firearms and explosives off the back of his deck as a celebration, before the police arrive, join the party, and place bets on his equally illegal mutant animal pit fighting ring?&quot;. The Seers don't just offer you freedom from want; they offer you the grandest heights the world has to offer. They are outright Satan standing with Christ on the Quarantania and offering all the kingdoms of the world.<br /> <br /> All of that comes from denying other people the same opportunities; from creating rules that apply to all and then exempting yourself from them. That is the very essence of tyranny.<br /> <br /> All the tools, all the Mysteries that Seers get access to, exist in service of those goals. These Mysteries are not idle things, preserved &quot;because&quot;. They exist as tools to enslave the world.<br /> <br /> Tyranny <i>is</i> the yantra <i>and</i> the spell. It is the means and the end; the purpose and the method. The two cannot be separated anymore than the Exarchs can from the actions of which they are the symbol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T22:20:39-08:00","id":1021149,"title":"","content":":') <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a>, they should have sent a poet...because that was beautiful. That is the summation of everything I love about the Seers of the Throne as both antagonists and as a fully playable Order. <br /> <br /> The only thing I would like to remind people is that the Exarch's marching orders tend to be very cryptic, as most moves in the Ascension War tend to be, with the exceptions of the Greater Ministers and the Prelates. That's why they value those who can successfully interpret the will of the Tyrants, and why many of their Orders Mysteries revolve around actually understanding what their Exarch commands them to do. Because if they don't...oooooh, that's where the fun stuff comes in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 12-23-2016, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T00:15:50-08:00","id":1021179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1021130#post1021130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to address your whole post but this feels like a good summary of it so I'm gonna save space on quoting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Holy moly... man I am glad I asked this question. This... this is why Mage is a horror game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11932-jerkajerka","name":"jerkajerka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T04:43:51-08:00","id":1021224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1021130#post1021130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that reason, tyranny <i>is</i> a goal, because the Exarchs seek tyranny.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope, not buying it. Too simplistic- the Exarchs aren't one dimensional like that.<br /> <br /> Even if we assume that the Exarchs are all Supernal Symbols, it doesn't change that they're seeking tyranny for a reason. To maintain their status as living magic symbols, perhaps - if tyranny disappeared, they'd stop existing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially since you're creating a hard line about what the Exarchs are or are not. That's no longer true in 2e. The entire premisis of your argument is flawed from the word go. </div> </div> </div> *sigh* Says the person who's created a hard line about the Exarchs being tyranny itself, and foster tyranny for that reason alone. I created a list of possibilities and explained how different interpretations would have Exarchs acting in different ways. You're the one who's made the hard line here, Axel. I'm arguing for a wider interpretation of the Exarchs being just being a magic spell of oppression*, perpetuating itself. Glass houses and stones, Axel.<br /> <br /> Lets assume, for a minute, that the Seers are right and the Exarchs are all ascended mages. Still a possibility here. <i>Why</i> did they become symbols of tyranny? They had an underlying reason for it. There's a reason they became that way, they had their Obsessions and Addictions like all other mages. Now, lets assume for a minute that the Father isn't a former archmage, but the God-Machine's attempts to put Infrastructure in the Supernal. The G-M uses oppression to acomplish an ultimate Mission it has in mind. Now, lets look at a third possibility - there never was a war in heaven, and the Exarchs were always Supernal Symbols and that alone. Much like spirits, Supernal Symbols need to strengthen their symbol in the Phenomenal World to have power in the Supernal. Cut away the source of their power, and they literally die out, ceasing to exist. The goal isn't tyarnny, the goal is maintaining life as a symbol. Now, lets pretend, for a moment, that the Exarchs are all coming from different sources.<br /> <br /> Irregardless of the form that an Exarch will take in any given chronicle, there's reasons behind being oppressive. Unless you deliberately <i>make</i> tyanny the goal, but that's going to be up to individual tables to decide, not cannon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether that tyranny makes them more powerful or not is anyone's guess </div> </div> </div> Right after you argue about them fostering tyranny because they are Supernal tyranny. That's how Supernal magic works - by strengthening tyanny in the world, they strengthen the Symbol as well. You can't have it both ways.<br /> <br /> <br /> * The Exarchs are called symbols of oppression, not tyranny. Tyranny is formed through oppressive governments and Ministries, and not all Exarchs have those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-23-2016, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T05:15:34-08:00","id":1021232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1021224#post1021224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nope, not buying it.<br /> <br /> Even if we assume that the Exarchs are all Supernal Symbols, it doesn't change that they're seeking tyranny for a reason. To maintain their status as living magic symbols, perhaps - if tyranny disappeared, they'd stop existing.<br /> <br /> *sigh* Says the person who's created a hard line about the Exarchs being tyranny itself, and foster tyranny for that reason alone. I created a list of possibilities and explained how different interpretations would have Exarchs acting in different ways. You're the one who's made the hard line here, Axel. I'm arguing for a wider interpretation of the Exarchs that can include things like the story hook of the Dark Mother possibly being the Raptor, as teased in BtP. There's far more to D.M. than just being a magic spell of tyranny.<br /> <br /> Right after you argue about them fostering tyranny because they are Supernal tyranny. That's how Supernal magic works - by strengthening tyanny in the world, they strengthen the Symbol as well. You can't have it both ways</div> </div> </div> </div>But Exarchs <b>are </b>Supernal symbols. Living ones, in fact. For whom action and intent are one and the same, which is a big theme of Supernal magic in general.<br /> <br /> There's no meaningful distinction between an Exarch thinking, &quot;I need to maintain my status as a living symbol' and &quot;I will foster my brand of tyranny upon the Fallen World&quot;. They are one and the same for that Exarch. To say that the former reason is different from the latter is to say they aren't living concepts, but just a reflection of that concept. We already have Rank 6+ spirits for that.<br /> <br /> And sorry to say this, MCN, but saying that the Exarchs are actually one or more of the cosmic god-forces in other gamelines seem less like a creative interpretation of the game, and more a reversal of that &quot;All gamelines are shadows of the Mage cosmology&quot; thing we had before that some Mage players insisted on. This particular &quot;hard line&quot;, where Exarchs are Supernal gods of Tyranny, is mor of a setting statement needed to pin the game down with consistency. And I don't think even the Crossover Chronicles we're all anticipating will trample one gameline's setting in favor of another - afterall, we had Mage developers clearly saying that Supernal Arcadia and Changeling Arcadia are not one and the same? If we go. &quot;Oh, the God-Machine is actually the Father&quot; or &quot;Oh, the Psychopomp manifests as a Rank 9 kerberos&quot;, then we can say &quot;Ah-hah, so the Gentry are Supernal Entities of Arcadia! Pssh, changelings aren't so important in the grand scheme after all!&quot; or &quot;Ah-hah, Pangaeans really are earth-bound Superna Entities of the Primal Wild!&quot; That is one thing I dread the most in any sort of Crossover material.<br /> <br /> Oh, and about the Dark Mother and the Raptor. We know that some mages claim that the Begotten must be of the Raptor, because the former are primordial fear-creatures and the latter is the symbol of control through fear of the wilderness. This is cannot be the same as saying that the Dark Mother and the Raptor are one and the same. It's just that the Dark Mother and her Begotten are patterns of the Fallen World that resonate strongly with the Supernal symbol that is the Raptor. The Primordial Dream resonates with many other symbols other than the Raptor, and the Raptor resonates with many other patterns than the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> About &quot;strengthening&quot;. Like I said, Supernal gods do not act. They exist. Whether this continued act of existence counts as 'strengthening' themselves is a semantics problem. Do we strengthen ourselves by breathing, eating and drinking? Normally, we don't. But the nutrients we consume build our muscles and facilitate our hormone and nervous systems, so does it count as 'strengthening' our bodies? If you put it that way, well yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T05:25:09-08:00","id":1021235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1021232#post1021232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And sorry to say this, MCN, but saying that the Exarchs are actually one or more of the cosmic god-forces in other gamelines seem less like a creative interpretation of the game, and more a reversal of that &quot;All gamelines are shadows of the Mage cosmology&quot; thing we had before that some Mage players insisted on.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm pulling directly from the books, not making that up. Check out Beast the Primordial where it talks about Mage crossover. Its cannon that there are a number of mages that believe that the Dark Mother is the Raptor. <br /> <br /> You don't like it? Not a problem. However <i>its directly in the books. </i>Its openly presented as a possibility. You'll have to take your complaints up with the writers, not me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T05:30:37-08:00","id":1021238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1021235#post1021235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm pulling directly from the books, not making that up. Check out Beast the Primordial where it talks about Mage crossover. Its cannon that there are a number of mages that believe that the Dark Mother is the Raptor.<br /> <br /> You don't like it? Not a problem. However <i>its directly in the books. </i>Its openly presented as a possibility. You'll have to take your complaints up with the writers, not me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, some mages believe so. In-universe. I also remember there being a Free Council Legacy whose members believe, in-universe, that the workings of Awakened magic change with what humanity believes in, just like it did in Mage the Ascension and its Consensus. What the book says on things that in-universe characters believe in do not equal what the book says on things that are true for that gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T05:59:46-08:00","id":1021243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1021238#post1021238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, some mages believe so. In-universe. I also remember there being a Free Council Legacy whose members believe, in-universe, that the workings of Awakened magic change with what humanity believes in, just like it did in Mage the Ascension and its Consensus. What the book says on things that in-universe characters believe in do not equal what the book says on things that are true for that gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually just the Free Council in general, but not like Consensus in Ascension. It's because as humanity changes it draws closer to or distances itself from symbols in the Supernal and the metaphysical distance can determine the usefulness of the symbol for performing magic.<br /> <br /> That said, yeah, I don't agree with you either MCN.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T08:47:49-08:00","id":1021287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1021224#post1021224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nope, not buying it. Too simplistic- the Exarchs aren't one dimensional like that.<br /> <br /> Even if we assume that the Exarchs are all Supernal Symbols, it doesn't change that they're seeking tyranny for a reason. To maintain their status as living magic symbols, perhaps - if tyranny disappeared, they'd stop existing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter is speculation. It might not even be possible for the Exarchs to vanish; the mere possibility of control through violence lets thwm exist.<br /> <br /> I think you're also conflating purity with a baser simplicity, and assuming that said purity means a lack of both internal complexity of the being and external complexity of action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1018603-why-are-the-seers-such-a-big-deal?p=1021224#post1021224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-rest of post-</div> </div> </div> </div>There's stuff for me to reply to here, and I will when I'm not out shopping, but you were quoting someone other than me there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T11:45:29-08:00","id":1021353,"title":"","content":"I can buy the &quot;control/power&quot; argument and the &quot;above the law&quot; argument, but I've never really bought into the wealth argument for why someone would want to be a Seer.<br /> <br /> IMO, any Mage can be rich if they want to. The Seers can't police everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T12:31:00-08:00","id":1021363,"title":"","content":"Which is why Axel pointed out it's not just about wealth, it's about privilege.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T15:25:07-08:00","id":1021414,"title":"","content":"I swear this thread is a gold mine! <br /> <br /> With both of your permission Axelgear &amp; MCN, may I borrow your arguments to use in game as a philosophical argument between two Seers? I can just imagine a Paternoster Seer (Exarchs are Tyranny's purest expression) and a Panopticon Seer (Exarchs have motivations beyond self existing as Tyranny) having this discussion and it would be such a cool in-game conundrum to introduce to the players. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T16:37:21-08:00","id":1021435,"title":"","content":"It's worth pointing out that the concept of Exarchs originated as a hypothesis. The Awakened originally only guessed the existence of the Exarchs based on what they saw happening in the world. Then the proto-Seers went and found them. Which, as far as I'm aware, is an untold story in the canon. There isn't anything that actually <i>requires</i> that the Exarchs are Supernal symbols; that's just the best interpretation because it works both for Watsonian (e.g., Mages who are unaware that there are non-Supernal things) and Doylist (e.g., wanting a gameline that works without crossover) analyses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T18:53:57-08:00","id":1021453,"title":"","content":"Mages are perfectly aware that there are non-Supernal things. That's actually the main source of their Mysteries which is why Signs of Sorcery is devoted to Supernal Mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T21:41:53-08:00","id":1021472,"title":"","content":"Something worth adding is that when a Mage says they think, say, that the Dark Mother is the Raptor, they're <i>probably</i> actually saying they believe the reverse.<br /> <br /> I want to expand on my note earlier about purity of motive.<br /> <br /> There's a concept in theology called Divine Simplicity. It's big in Aristotle and bigger in Aquinas (who basically saw Aristotle and felt he was great but needed a lot more Jesus). It's a concept over which wars have been fought, so I am not going to be able to summarize it or comment on it tremendously effectively or do the topic justice in a forum post, but it's a critical note here.<br /> <br /> Divine simplicity is the idea that God is solely defined by its own nature. It has no other dependencies. It does what it does not because outside powers make or made it do so, but because it is in its nature to do them. It is self-defining, existing purely in reference to itself, and graspable by mortal minds only through allegory and relation. There are no divisions to its nature; no separate parts which war with one another. Its whole being acts in concert, rather than warring with itself as per humans.<br /> <br /> The important part of divine simplicity is that it in no way denies complexity in the common sense. A divinely simple being is, indeed, staggeringly complex, for it encompasses so much of existence in its nature. It also, however, emphasizes something else: That there is a purity in its motive. When God acts a certain way, it does so ultimately because it is God. There is no grander motive because there can <i>be</i> no grander motive. Ultimately, this is true of humans too; we can make grand plans but our ultimate motives can be stated simply. We just tend to have more than one motive, and they are frequently at war.<br /> <br /> The Exarchs are Supernal symbols, and their tyrannical motive needing no further explanation than &quot;They're Exarchs&quot; is in keeping with a setting that treats Supernal symbols as divinely simple. It doesn't diminish, however, the complexity of the belief systems, ideologies, apologetics, structures, hierarchies, faiths, doctrines, or other codified obeisances that grow beneath them. The Exarchs can be, and are, staggeringly complex, even when their essence is simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}